  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square oil painting of hooded figures with pod shaped heads crowding below a chalkboard screen, while a purple helmeted figure stands on a platform at right.",
    "description": "A square oil painting on canvas. The lower half is a crowd of hooded figures seen from behind, each a rounded pod shape in olive, orange, blue, pink and green with a visor like opening and heavy black outlines. They face a large framed panel at upper left that shows an interior scene of a figure in a doorway with a globe above it, like a screen or a window. At upper right, a figure in a purple hooded suit with a smiling face stands on a raised platform, pointing, beside a wall with a clock and dials. The space between is divided into coloured panels. Brushwork is visible and the palette is muted purple, olive and orange.",
    "impression": "A lesson is happening and the class is a crowd of identical hooded pupils, all turned toward the screen. The teacher on the platform looks like an astronaut cheerleader. It plays on the strangeness of a room full of backs of heads, which is what school looks like from the back row.",
